     "content": "The user wants me to act as a Skeptic and evaluate the crime link between CHN-GU-2025-001149 and CHN-ST-2025-001108. I need to decide: approve, send_back, or drop.\n\nLet me analyze the pair:\n\nCrime A (Guindy): cab_robbery, 2025-10-07 01:09, near Hilton Chennai, Guindy\n- Vehicle: white Maruti Swift Dzire, plate null\n- 3 offenders, heavy build, age 25-35\n- Weapon: knife\n- MO: posed_as_ride_hailing_cab, drove_away_in_car, hotel_nearby_or_parking, target late_night_passenger, cash_and_mobile_phone, night, knife_shown_to_threaten\n\nCrime B (St. Thomas Mount): cab_robbery, 2025-09-27 00:30, near Saint Thomas Mount, St. Thomas Mount\n- Vehicle: white Maruti Swift Dzire, plate null\n- 3 offenders, heavy build, age 25-35\n- Weapon: knife\n- MO: null\n\nDistance: 2.3 km, Days apart: 10.0\nFactors: space_time (0.27), vehicle (0.5), suspect_description (1.0), weapon_tool (1.0)\nScore: 0.6317, band: medium, coverage: 0.5\n\nKey observations:\n- Both are cab_robbery category\n- 2.3 km apart - close geographically\n- 10 days apart - reasonable for a series\n- Both night time (01:09 and 00:30)\n- Both used white Maruti Swift Dzire, but NO PLATE for either\n- Vehicle factor is only 0.5 because plates are null - the ANPR-R0285340 provides some trail evidence but no plate match\n- Suspect description IDENTICAL: 3 offenders, heavy build, age 25-35\n- Weapon: both knife\n- MO missing for Crime B - this is a significant gap\n- Coverage only 0.5 (4 of 8 factors)\n\nAs a Skeptic, I need to be strict. The identical suspect description (3 heavy-build males 25-35) is somewhat generic - could be a common description. The vehicle match is only make/model/color with no plate. The MO is missing for Crime B. The space_time score is only 0.27 (moderate).\n\nHowever, the combination of: same crime type (cab_robbery), same vehicle make/model/color, identical suspect description, same weapon, close proximity (2.3 km), close time (10 days), both night - this is quite compelling